# Ready-made Firefox profiles (extras/firefox-profiles/new-profile.sh NAME, or
# --list). Each is made only when you ask for it: a locked-down user of its own
# (fx-NAME) and a command, NAME (firefox-NAME when a program is called NAME).
#
# NAME URL FAST-JS TOOLBARS SOUND COOKIES ALLOW # what it is
#   FAST-JS   yes: the JavaScript JIT on for this profile (heavy apps, video, chess)
#   TOOLBARS  hidden (only the page) or shown (where seeing the address matters)
#   SOUND     yes or no
#   COOKIES   keep (stay logged in) or delete (gone when it closes)
#   ALLOW     sites ublock-allow opens to scripts and frames from other sites
#             (uBlock's medium mode blocks those, and these sites load their own
#             code from a second domain: GitHub from githubassets.com, YouTube from
#             ytimg.com...), comma-separated; - for none. Checked 2026-11-05 from
#             each site's page; one that still breaks: ublock-allow SITE.
#
# Mail
tutamail https://app.tuta.com no hidden no keep - # Tuta (Tutanota) mail, end-to-end encrypted
protonmail https://mail.proton.me no hidden no keep - # Proton Mail, end-to-end encrypted
gmail https://mail.google.com no hidden no keep mail.google.com # Gmail
yahoomail https://mail.yahoo.com no hidden no keep mail.yahoo.com # Yahoo Mail
outlook https://outlook.live.com no hidden no keep outlook.live.com # Outlook.com mail
# AI chat
duckai https://duck.ai no hidden no delete - # DuckDuckGo's AI chat: no account, nothing kept
claudefx https://claude.ai no hidden no keep claude.ai # Claude on the web (claude is Claude Code's command)
chatgpt https://chatgpt.com no hidden no keep chatgpt.com # ChatGPT
lechat https://chat.mistral.ai no hidden no keep - # Mistral's Le Chat
# Code
github https://github.com no shown no keep github.com # GitHub
gitlab https://gitlab.com no shown no keep - # GitLab
codeberg https://codeberg.org no shown no keep - # Codeberg, a non-profit Git host
stackoverflow https://stackoverflow.com no shown no delete stackoverflow.com # Stack Overflow
# Video
youtube https://www.youtube.com yes hidden yes delete youtube.com # YouTube, forgotten when it closes
odysee https://odysee.com yes hidden yes delete odysee.com # Odysee
peertube https://framatube.org yes hidden yes delete - # PeerTube (Framasoft's; other instances work too)
# Adult
pornhub https://www.pornhub.com no hidden yes delete pornhub.com # forgotten when it closes
xvideos https://www.xvideos.com no hidden yes delete xvideos.com # forgotten when it closes
# Games
chess https://www.chess.com yes hidden yes delete chess.com # Chess.com, forgotten when it closes
lichess https://lichess.org yes hidden yes delete - # Lichess, free and open source chess
# Social: each company's trackers see only their own site
facebook https://www.facebook.com no hidden yes keep facebook.com # Facebook
instagram https://www.instagram.com no hidden yes keep instagram.com # Instagram
xcom https://x.com no hidden yes keep x.com # X (Twitter)
reddit https://www.reddit.com no hidden yes keep reddit.com # Reddit
linkedin https://www.linkedin.com no hidden no keep linkedin.com # LinkedIn
mastodon https://mastodon.social no hidden yes keep - # Mastodon (mastodon.social; change it to your own server)
# Chat
discord https://discord.com/app yes hidden yes keep discord.com # Discord
element https://app.element.io yes hidden yes keep - # Element (Matrix), end-to-end encrypted
whatsapp https://web.whatsapp.com yes hidden yes keep web.whatsapp.com # WhatsApp Web
# Shopping: their trackers kept to themselves
amazon https://www.amazon.com no shown no keep amazon.com # Amazon
ebay https://www.ebay.com no shown no keep ebay.com # eBay
# Reference
archive https://archive.org no shown yes delete - # The Internet Archive and its Wayback Machine
osm https://www.openstreetmap.org no shown no delete - # OpenStreetMap
search https://duckduckgo.com no shown no delete - # DuckDuckGo search, nothing kept between searches
